$$
40\sqrt{5} = s \cdot \sqrt{\frac{11}{6}}
$$

Now solve for $ s $:

$$
s = \frac{40\sqrt{5}}{\sqrt{\frac{11}{6}}} = \frac{40\sqrt{5}}{\frac{\sqrt{11}}{\sqrt{6}}} = \frac{40\sqrt{5} \cdot \sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{11}} = \frac{40\sqrt{30}}{\sqrt{11}}
